femto patch for epub-stream 0.1.0
Subject: zip: open archives as books in circulation are made

Two limits refused books that other reading systems open. Found by opening
all 110 EPUBs of one library: four did not open for these reasons.

1. validate_mimetype required the entry to be exactly
   "application/epub+zip". Two books end it with a line break. Trailing
   spaces, tabs and line breaks are now accepted; anything before or
   within the type is still refused. Adds a unit test.
2. The central directory cache held 256 entries, and entries past that
   were not found. Two illustrated books have 302 and 437. The cache now
   holds 2048; an entry is about a hundred bytes on the heap.

The manifest also enables the escape-html feature of quick-xml, so that
HTML named entities such as &nbsp; resolve. Six books use them in XHTML
and their chapters did not parse. That change is in Cargo.toml, which is
rewritten by hand and not part of this diff.

Upstreamable: all three.

